# PM11: Seq tail must not be forced when the body only accesses the head.
# The tail contains a raise — if the tail were forced eagerly, this would error.
# T-1154: [Seq h _] no longer binds h; use [Seq.Cons p] to bind the payload dict.
# p.tail is never accessed — the raise must not fire.
[match [seq 42 [raise "tail must not be forced"]]
  [case [let p] [Seq.Cons p] p.head]
  ...:                       0]
=== out
Int(42)
